odon/Bluesky) linked","pass":false,"detail":""}],"passed":8,"total":11,"social":[],"og":{"title":"Center for Digital Twins in Manufacturing (CDTM)","description":"A collaboration between the University of Michigan and Arizona State University, the Center is focused on developing digital twin (DT) solutions for manufacturing. The potential benefits of the Center's research are significant and expansive. Improvements in re-usability, extensibility, interoperability and maintainability of solutions will improve manufacturing throughput and quality and reduce cost directly. Key DT framework capabilities such as virtual commissioning will facilitate faster and lower-cost ramp-up, while cutting edge research will explore the ways in which AI and machine learning can accelerate the modeling, estimation and prediction capabilities of DTs. A common framework will allow the benefits to extend to the entire manufacturing ecosystem and will enhance capabilities such as security and customer responsiveness. Lastly, the Center will promote workforce development and empowerment by establishing environments and solutions for training (including the appropriate usage of AI/ML), benchmarking and collaboration between competitors, suppliers, and customers in a technical, pre-competitive forum.","url":"/centers/center-for-digital-twins-in-manufacturing/","image":"/assets/images/twittercard.png","siteName":null,"type":"article"},"resilience":{"checks":[{"id":"pwa-https","label":"HTTPS (required for service workers)","status":"pass","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-digital-twins-in-manufacturing/","why":"HTTPS is required for service workers and most install prompts."},{"id":"pwa-manifest","label":"Web app manifest declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-digital-twins-in-manufacturing/","why":"A web app manifest is required for installability and controls how the app appears when launched."},{"id":